Create a new location block in your main `server` block that will handle links to individual posts. You'll need to add a `location` block that matches the URL pattern for each post, and then use the `try_files` directive to serve the corresponding HTML file.

For example, you can add the following code:
```makefile
location ~ ^/posts/.+\.(html|htm)$ {
    try_files $uri $uri/ /posts/$uri.html;
    index index.html;
}
```
This code will match any URL that starts with `/posts/` and has an extension of `.html` or `.htm`. If a matching file is found, Nginx will serve it. If not, it will fall back to serving the `index.html` file from the `/posts` directory.

